    <fr:title text="Interpretation of a Quiver into a Category">Interpretation of a Quiver into a Category</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Given a <fr:link href="/sss-0066/" title="Quiver" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0066/" display-uri="sss-0066" type="local">Quiver</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex> and a category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex>, an
<html:em>interpretation of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex> in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex></html:em>, written
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\iota  : Q \rightsquigarrow  C]]></fr:tex>, is a graph homomorphism from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex> into the
underlying graph of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
    <html:p>Likewise, for a displayed category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex> we can define a <html:em>displayed interpretation of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[Q]]></fr:tex> in
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[C^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex></html:em> in a straightforward manner, written <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\iota ^{\mathtt {D}} : Q \rightsquigarrow  C^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
